  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd a disk-backed regression to the existing `default_machine_missing` suite.\nThe test calls `default_machine_checked` in one isolated child process.\nIt reads `assets/machines/3axis-vmc.mch` beside a copied test executable.\nThe sequence is a missing file, `{}`, and the good shipped file.\nThe results must be `Err`, `Err`, `Ok` without a restart.\nA later broken file must not replace the good parsed machine.\n\n## Why\n\nThe existing `KeptMachine` test supplies its own reader.\nIt cannot detect a text cache in `default_mch_text`.\nProduction already has the correct behavior. This PR changes no production code, machine file, or posting rule.\nThe new test joins the existing suite. It adds no integration binary or dependency.\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/2324-default-machine-disk-pin.md`.\n\n## Verification\n\nTest: `disk_recovery::a_repaired_default_machine_file_is_read_again_through_the_disk_reader`.\n\n- Baseline: the new test passes with the current disk reader.\n- Mutation: temporarily cache each successful text read in `default_mch_text` with `OnceLock<String>`.\n  Missing reads still retry, but the cache keeps `{}`. The new test fails at the repaired-file assertion:\n  `the repaired file must be read without a restart`.\n  The refusal reports `it has no machine name`. The command exits with status 1.\n- Restoration: restore the original production file byte-for-byte. The new test passes again.\n- Final head: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` passes the complete `default_machine_missing` suite: 10 passed, 0 failed.\n- Final head: `cargo clippy -j 3 -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\n- `rustfmt --check --edition 2024 crates/app/tests/default_machine_missing/disk_recovery.rs` passes.\n- `git diff --check` passes. No cache mutation remains in this diff.\n\nThe focused baseline, mutation, and restoration command was:\n\n```sh\ncargo xtask gate test disk_recovery::a_repaired_default_machine_file_is_read_again_through_the_disk_reader --crate camcraft-app --binary default_machine_missing --exact\n```\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Light lane: NOT RUN. It uses release mode, which conflicts with the bounded debug-only validation scope for this test-only change.\n- Catalog, heavy, release, full-workspace, and GUI lanes: NOT RUN. No post script, toolpath, or production behavior changes.\n- Windows and macOS: NOT RUN. Execution evidence is from Linux.\n- No physical-machine safety or real posting certification is claimed.\n- GitHub checks are reported separately. Local results are not a CI result.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #2324\n",
